294
00:13:10,290 --> 00:13:13,500
Next life, you'll understand

295
00:13:13,500 --> 00:13:16,030
I want to say

296
00:13:16,030 --> 00:13:19,560
if our roles were reversed

297
00:13:19,560 --> 00:13:25,110
I'd beg you to shoot, no hesitation

298
00:13:25,110 --> 00:13:34,430
Goodbye

299
00:13:34,430 --> 00:13:35,790
And then I died

300
00:13:35,790 --> 00:13:58,590
Next scene

301
00:13:58,590 --> 00:14:00,620
Anything else you want to say?

302
00:14:00,620 --> 00:14:03,060
Not now — there'll be a chance later

303
00:14:03,060 --> 00:14:04,660
Then hurry up and go

304
00:14:04,660 --> 00:14:08,440
Save it for the next act

305
00:14:08,440 --> 00:14:09,400
Come on, do the bit with the Boss

306
00:14:09,400 --> 00:14:10,920
Weren't we talking to the actors?

307
00:14:10,920 --> 00:14:13,960
Say whatever, just say whatever

308
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:15,240
Let him untie it

309
00:14:15,240 --> 00:14:16,560
I...

310
00:14:16,560 --> 00:14:18,480
Are you watching me?

311
00:14:18,480 --> 00:14:21,640
Do I look pretty on camera right now?

312
00:14:21,640 --> 00:14:23,800
But actually

313
00:14:23,800 --> 00:14:26,880
this is a completely fake face

314
00:14:26,880 --> 00:14:29,120
I could take all my makeup off

315
00:14:29,120 --> 00:14:30,600
and just sing along with you

316
00:14:30,600 --> 00:14:33,040
It's always me who finds the time

317
00:14:33,040 --> 00:14:35,320
It's not like I'm after something

318
00:14:35,320 --> 00:14:37,000
You come out and it just isn't there

319
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:39,320
Get all fired up, then come back out

320
00:14:39,320 --> 00:14:41,320
I've bought out all these

321
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:43,320
people trying to talk me into leaving

322
00:14:44,600 --> 00:14:46,640
Mic

323
00:14:46,640 --> 00:14:48,080
Iceberg, Act One

324
00:14:48,080 --> 00:14:49,970
No music

325
00:14:49,970 --> 00:15:03,430
Improvised performance

326
00:15:03,430 --> 00:15:04,790
I know you're home

327
00:15:04,790 --> 00:15:06,710
Pay up or I'm telling your neighbors

328
00:15:06,710 --> 00:15:08,070
I'll go to your workplace

329
00:15:08,070 --> 00:15:09,670
and let all your coworkers know

330
00:15:09,670 --> 00:15:11,270
You hear me?

331
00:15:11,270 --> 00:15:13,390
Unbelievable, it's just three grand

332
00:15:13,390 --> 00:15:14,110
and you keep stalling

333
00:15:14,110 --> 00:15:15,070
You'll never amount to anything

334
00:15:15,070 --> 00:15:26,710
You're finished, fuck your mother

335
00:15:26,710 --> 00:15:28,390
That's way too blinding

336
00:15:45,260 --> 00:16:01,840
What's going through your head here?

337
00:16:01,840 --> 00:16:03,400
Is there music playing in your head?

338
00:16:03,400 --> 00:16:04,520
Which tune?

339
00:16:13,460 --> 00:16:14,460
Indescribable

340
00:16:26,860 --> 00:16:27,500
In this part

341
00:16:27,500 --> 00:16:30,500
I feel like a puddle of water

342
00:16:30,500 --> 00:16:32,860
just rotting away right here

343
00:16:32,860 --> 00:16:33,860
Turned to mist

344
00:16:37,280 --> 00:16:39,120
Water? That's still too clean

345
00:16:39,120 --> 00:16:40,320
Go a few steps further

346
00:16:40,320 --> 00:16:41,880
All see-through

347
00:16:41,880 --> 00:16:43,280
A Ditto

348
00:16:45,820 --> 00:16:46,620
Just to mention

349
00:16:46,620 --> 00:16:48,300
I mean

350
00:16:48,300 --> 00:16:49,820
It's in this

351
00:16:49,820 --> 00:16:51,140
muddy kind of state

352
00:16:51,140 --> 00:16:55,480
A state where you can't even die properly

353
00:16:55,480 --> 00:16:57,080
Every day we can fantasize

354
00:16:57,080 --> 00:16:58,880
about us and the brutal Boss

355
00:16:58,880 --> 00:17:00,160
The Boss is like a

356
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:02,480
how do I put it

357
00:17:02,800 --> 00:17:04,600
It's a slave-and-master relationship

358
00:17:04,600 --> 00:17:05,840
Say the Boss is the master

359
00:17:05,840 --> 00:17:07,400
whipping you all day

360
00:17:07,400 --> 00:17:08,840
That's not the kind...

361
00:17:09,680 --> 00:17:11,360
Rather, it's through certain

362
00:17:11,360 --> 00:17:12,560
subtle, unnoticed things

363
00:17:12,560 --> 00:17:14,440
that he reshapes your perception

364
00:17:14,720 --> 00:17:16,440
He just thinks your perception is wrong

365
00:17:18,250 --> 00:17:19,370
That's the state he's in

366
00:17:19,370 --> 00:17:20,890
But the Male Lead feels

367
00:17:20,890 --> 00:17:22,530
on one hand, the people around him

368
00:17:22,530 --> 00:17:24,290
treat him decently enough

369
00:17:24,290 --> 00:17:25,650
so why does he always feel, deep down,

370
00:17:25,650 --> 00:17:26,610
there's something strange

371
00:17:26,610 --> 00:17:28,810
something a little off?

372
00:17:28,810 --> 00:17:29,570
And that wrongness

373
00:17:29,570 --> 00:17:32,570
keeps itching, scratching, picking at him

374
00:17:32,570 --> 00:17:34,770
Everything the Male Lead does on stage

375
00:17:34,770 --> 00:17:37,180
as long as it's set in his own home

376
00:17:37,180 --> 00:17:39,060
anything set in his own home

377
00:17:39,060 --> 00:17:41,860
is his inner world acted outward

378
00:17:41,860 --> 00:17:45,220
Meaning if you saw him there in person

379
00:17:45,220 --> 00:17:48,060
he'd really just be sitting here

380
00:17:48,060 --> 00:17:48,900
Just like this

381
00:17:48,900 --> 00:18:01,580
It's too fucking dark

382
00:18:01,580 --> 00:18:04,900
Heads or tails — I can never tell

383
00:18:04,900 --> 00:18:07,220
Everyone loves to watch heads

384
00:18:07,220 --> 00:18:09,580
The day the heads people slip up

385
00:18:09,580 --> 00:18:12,500
the tails people start to revel

386
00:18:12,500 --> 00:18:15,340
When the tails side errs, the heads side

387
00:18:15,340 --> 00:18:18,670
what do they get to see?

388
00:18:18,670 --> 00:18:22,370
It's like one group of people is here

389
00:18:22,370 --> 00:18:23,250
one person is here

390
00:18:23,250 --> 00:18:24,730
and another one over here

391
00:18:24,730 --> 00:18:26,890
It's even like, you know

392
00:18:26,890 --> 00:18:29,490
it simply can't find

393
00:18:29,490 --> 00:18:32,810
one tone that holds from start to finish

394
00:18:32,810 --> 00:18:35,180
That's the most fatal problem

395
00:18:35,180 --> 00:18:36,860
Before I went on stage

396
00:18:36,860 --> 00:18:39,420
I didn't even dare to perform

397
00:18:39,420 --> 00:18:40,460
Honestly speaking

398
00:18:40,460 --> 00:18:42,420
Two days before going on

399
00:18:42,420 --> 00:18:45,250
I told playwright Shi I shouldn't go on

400
00:18:45,250 --> 00:18:47,130
because I felt this thing

401
00:18:47,130 --> 00:18:49,450
was the worst I've ever acted in

402
00:18:49,450 --> 00:18:51,660
the shittiest, trashiest thing ever

403
00:18:51,660 --> 00:18:52,260
Really?

404
00:18:52,260 --> 00:18:54,780
I mean

405
00:18:54,780 --> 00:18:55,460
Really

406
00:18:55,460 --> 00:18:57,500
Anyway, with my own performance

407
00:18:57,500 --> 00:18:59,920
I'm deeply unsatisfied

408
00:18:59,920 --> 00:19:02,360
How I wish they were like you

409
00:19:02,360 --> 00:19:03,760
with only one side

410
00:19:03,760 --> 00:19:06,540
only able to see themselves

411
00:19:06,540 --> 00:19:08,060
Scraping by in the concrete jungle

412
00:19:08,060 --> 00:19:10,450
has stunted people's thinking

413
00:19:10,450 --> 00:19:12,530
A person has ten units of energy a day

414
00:19:12,530 --> 00:19:14,170
Work burns five

415
00:19:14,170 --> 00:19:16,450
dealing with people takes three

416
00:19:16,450 --> 00:19:21,690
the last two get wasted on fun

417
00:19:21,690 --> 00:19:24,240
I've spared myself all that pondering

418
00:19:24,240 --> 00:19:36,540
I even plan to quit this hypocritical job

419
00:19:36,540 --> 00:19:38,810
Let me ask you a question

420
00:19:38,810 --> 00:19:42,600
Would you get a reaction on stage?

421
00:19:42,600 --> 00:19:43,840
What do you think?

422
00:19:43,840 --> 00:19:44,560
Just guessing

423
00:19:44,560 --> 00:19:46,720
You think getting a reaction on stage

424
00:19:46,720 --> 00:19:48,760
is something that can happen?

425
00:19:48,760 --> 00:19:51,080
I think it can

426
00:19:51,080 --> 00:19:52,560
One look at you and it goes soft

427
00:19:52,560 --> 00:19:57,410
Are you talking to me?

428
00:19:57,410 --> 00:20:05,260
Being understood is just too hard

429
00:20:05,260 --> 00:20:08,320
I thought you knew

430
00:20:08,320 --> 00:20:10,420
I go the long way to you every day

431
00:20:10,420 --> 00:20:12,420
always right when you're on shift

432
00:20:12,420 --> 00:20:14,420
Yet you don't even know

433
00:20:14,420 --> 00:20:20,380
what cigarettes I smoke

434
00:20:20,380 --> 00:20:21,380
I...

435
00:20:21,380 --> 00:20:24,790
You don't know me at all, do you?

436
00:20:24,790 --> 00:20:26,790
All my love is right here

437
00:20:26,790 --> 00:20:29,370
and you never even knew

438
00:20:29,370 --> 00:20:42,510
Only this way would you notice me

439
00:20:42,510 --> 00:20:52,520
Being noticed is just too hard

440
00:20:52,520 --> 00:20:57,300
It's just too hard

441
00:20:57,300 --> 00:20:58,140
He's the playwright

442
00:20:58,140 --> 00:21:02,740
His head is full of water

443
00:21:02,740 --> 00:21:04,220
Hey, you upstairs

444
00:21:04,220 --> 00:21:07,470
Play something else, will you?

445
00:21:07,470 --> 00:21:11,440
Can you do Bach?

446
00:21:11,440 --> 00:21:12,760
Enough with Chopin

447
00:21:12,760 --> 00:21:17,240
Romanticism is dead

448
00:21:17,240 --> 00:21:20,050
Hey, do you hear me?

449
00:21:20,050 --> 00:21:22,390
Sha sha yi

450
00:21:22,390 --> 00:21:23,230
No — fuck

451
00:21:23,230 --> 00:21:24,540
Not in sync

452
00:21:24,540 --> 00:21:26,380
Three, two, one

453
00:21:26,380 --> 00:21:40,940
Sha sha yi

454
00:21:40,940 --> 00:21:42,860
These artists are always like this

455
00:21:42,860 --> 00:21:45,880
Won't face reality, won't die either

456
00:21:45,880 --> 00:21:47,600
It makes things hard for me

457
00:21:47,600 --> 00:21:50,200
Romanticism won't put food on the table

458
00:21:50,200 --> 00:21:50,800
If it could

459
00:21:50,800 --> 00:21:55,160
we might as well die at fantasy's climax

460
00:21:55,160 --> 00:21:58,030
But hey, it's artistic creation

461
00:21:58,030 --> 00:21:59,310
can't really fault it

462
00:21:59,310 --> 00:22:03,250
Too bad I just don't care for it

463
00:22:03,250 --> 00:22:08,320
Out of smokes

464
00:22:08,320 --> 00:22:10,150
Here you go

465
00:22:10,150 --> 00:22:11,950
Thanks

466
00:22:11,950 --> 00:22:14,230
A free pack of smokes

467
00:22:14,230 --> 00:22:15,350
Got cigarettes now

468
00:22:15,350 --> 00:22:16,750
But I can't smoke now

469
00:22:16,750 --> 00:22:20,090
No smoking in the theatre

470
00:22:20,090 --> 00:22:21,210
There's even a lighter

471
00:22:21,210 --> 00:22:22,650
Now the smokes are in your hands

472
00:22:22,650 --> 00:22:27,420
To smoke or not — that's up to you

473
00:22:27,420 --> 00:22:29,220
I get to see him again

474
00:22:29,220 --> 00:22:30,660
I really like him

475
00:22:30,660 --> 00:22:32,460
Though I've never spoken to him

476
00:22:32,460 --> 00:22:35,390
I just know he must be lovely

477
00:22:35,390 --> 00:22:38,030
Every day when I look out the window

478
00:22:38,030 --> 00:22:39,990
he's right there, busy at work

479
00:22:39,990 --> 00:22:40,750
In winter

480
00:22:40,750 --> 00:22:43,630
he wears a bright red scarf

481
00:22:43,630 --> 00:22:45,550
Her hair tucked into her scarf

482
00:22:45,550 --> 00:22:47,270
Makes her look so docile

483
00:22:47,270 --> 00:22:48,070
In summer

484
00:22:48,070 --> 00:22:50,350
Her sweat dampens her bangs

485
00:22:50,350 --> 00:22:54,210
She's too busy to even fix them

486
00:22:54,210 --> 00:22:57,210
But that's her truest, most beautiful self

487
00:22:57,210 --> 00:22:58,450
I really like her

488
00:22:58,450 --> 00:23:00,170
I believe this is my love

489
00:23:00,170 --> 00:23:02,410
I don't like the one who used to like me

490
00:23:02,410 --> 00:23:03,050
You know?

491
00:23:03,050 --> 00:23:04,690
She's always grinning

492
00:23:04,690 --> 00:23:06,210
Never takes what I say to heart

493
00:23:06,210 --> 00:23:08,590
I said, Sally

494
00:23:08,590 --> 00:23:10,470
I'm a sociologist now

495
00:23:10,470 --> 00:23:13,670
I've seen the ugly side of this society

496
00:23:13,670 --> 00:23:15,550
Look, isn't my dress pretty?

497
00:23:15,550 --> 00:23:17,910
But we're all living in lies

498
00:23:17,910 --> 00:23:19,070
Let's go shopping tomorrow

499
00:23:19,070 --> 00:23:22,070
I'll buy more, even prettier dresses

500
00:23:22,070 --> 00:23:22,430
Sally

501
00:23:22,430 --> 00:23:24,230
Do you really know my heart?

502
00:23:24,230 --> 00:23:26,310
Of course I do. So, you going or not?

503
00:23:26,310 --> 00:23:32,620
Sally, you're such a fucking idiot

504
00:23:32,620 --> 00:23:36,540
Look, if I slept with someone like her

505
00:23:36,540 --> 00:23:39,220
Uh, I mean, spent my life with her

506
00:23:39,220 --> 00:23:40,460
It'd be a tragedy for sure

507
00:23:40,460 --> 00:23:47,620
Calling you a fucking idiot

508
00:23:47,620 --> 00:23:49,100
Are you free tomorrow afternoon?

509
00:23:49,100 --> 00:23:50,900
I hear there's a good movie out

510
00:23:50,900 --> 00:23:53,030
You seen the movie? No?

511
00:23:53,030 --> 00:23:54,550
No, too abrupt

512
00:23:54,550 --> 00:24:00,550
Let me think

513
00:24:00,550 --> 00:24:03,700
Can I ask your name?

514
00:24:03,700 --> 00:24:05,780
Oh, what a lovely name

515
00:24:05,780 --> 00:24:14,990
No good

516
00:24:14,990 --> 00:24:16,710
Haven't we met somewhere?

517
00:24:16,710 --> 00:24:20,060
You look so familiar

518
00:24:20,060 --> 00:24:22,020
Too cliché

519
00:24:22,020 --> 00:24:23,220
I'd better just improvise

520
00:24:23,220 --> 00:24:36,280
I don't want these lines tying me down

521
00:24:36,280 --> 00:24:39,330
Iceberg, Act Two

522
00:24:39,330 --> 00:24:40,450
No lights, no sound

523
00:24:40,450 --> 00:24:41,330
Nothing at all

524
00:24:41,330 --> 00:24:42,010
All improvised

525
00:24:42,010 --> 00:24:42,970
Now that's interesting

526
00:24:45,330 --> 00:24:46,410
No thermal underwear

527
00:24:46,410 --> 00:24:48,680
It's freezing

528
00:24:48,680 --> 00:24:49,640
I'm not in the deep sea

529
00:24:49,640 --> 00:24:52,200
I'm in the glacier

530
00:24:55,680 --> 00:24:58,120
I feel out of place in this theatre

531
00:25:00,320 --> 00:25:02,280
As if drifting through the deep sea

532
00:25:03,400 --> 00:25:04,440
Funny thing

533
00:25:04,440 --> 00:25:06,480
The deep sea has neon lights too

534
00:25:06,480 --> 00:25:10,140
Sea creatures hunt with light

535
00:25:10,140 --> 00:25:14,460
The ocean is just like this theatre

536
00:25:14,460 --> 00:25:16,960
The deeper you go

537
00:25:16,960 --> 00:25:18,560
The fewer people there are

538
00:25:31,480 --> 00:25:39,100
This is, this is, this is—

539
00:25:39,100 --> 00:25:42,820
I... I'll take a pack of cigarettes

540
00:25:42,820 --> 00:25:49,200
Um, can I ask your name?

541
00:25:49,200 --> 00:25:50,080
No. Why?

542
00:25:50,080 --> 00:25:56,030
Just wanted to ask if you're free tomorrow

543
00:25:56,030 --> 00:25:56,910
I'm not free

544
00:25:56,910 --> 00:26:01,210
Then... then when are you free?

545
00:26:01,210 --> 00:26:03,810
Huh? Never

546
00:26:03,810 --> 00:26:08,300
You're my friend

547
00:26:08,300 --> 00:26:08,460
Hey

548
00:26:08,460 --> 00:26:12,490
How can you talk to a customer like that?

549
00:26:12,490 --> 00:26:15,730
The customer is your God

550
00:26:15,730 --> 00:26:17,530
Now God wants to know your name

551
00:26:17,530 --> 00:26:19,460
You dare not tell him?

552
00:26:19,460 --> 00:26:23,080
Do you dare?

553
00:26:23,080 --> 00:26:24,560
I just want to know your name

554
00:26:24,560 --> 00:26:31,900
Is that so hard?

555
00:26:31,900 --> 00:26:39,890
What are you hiding down there for?

556
00:26:39,890 --> 00:26:41,570
I'm a robber

557
00:26:41,570 --> 00:26:47,590
You think I'm a robber?

558
00:26:47,590 --> 00:27:06,620
You talking to me?

559
00:27:06,620 --> 00:27:09,160
The lighter's gone

560
00:27:09,160 --> 00:27:20,060
Kecheng

561
00:27:20,060 --> 00:27:23,130
What's it to you?

562
00:27:23,130 --> 00:27:32,720
You rat playwright

563
00:27:32,720 --> 00:27:34,160
An eight-yuan pack of smokes

564
00:27:34,160 --> 00:27:37,280
And he only gave me one yuan change

565
00:27:37,280 --> 00:27:40,700
Dignity's worth one yuan

566
00:27:40,700 --> 00:27:44,730
Maybe he's long known his soul's price

567
00:27:44,730 --> 00:27:45,690
If I were like him

568
00:27:45,690 --> 00:27:47,640
I'd go report him

569
00:27:47,640 --> 00:28:00,940
But I won't

570
00:28:00,940 --> 00:28:04,690
The best venue for this play is—

571
00:28:04,690 --> 00:28:05,970
It shouldn't be in a theatre like this

572
00:28:05,970 --> 00:28:08,530
It should be in some sewer

573
00:28:08,530 --> 00:28:11,210
With rats scurrying around

574
00:28:11,210 --> 00:28:12,570
Everyone sitting in a row

575
00:28:12,570 --> 00:28:13,770
Just watching it

576
00:28:13,770 --> 00:28:15,770
Watching this shitty play

577
00:28:15,770 --> 00:28:21,400
Other than that, it's...

578
00:28:21,400 --> 00:28:22,880
This, this script is way too cutesy

579
00:28:24,010 --> 00:28:24,730
Written way too cutesy

580
00:28:24,730 --> 00:28:25,370
Too young

581
00:28:25,370 --> 00:28:26,610
Too cute

582
00:28:26,610 --> 00:28:30,620
Sometimes the words that come out

583
00:28:30,620 --> 00:28:33,020
Make me feel it's not a...

584
00:28:34,900 --> 00:28:36,900
It's just not a grown-up script

585
00:28:36,900 --> 00:28:39,720
