Then it's on to the Boss's part

876
00:38:35,600 --> 00:38:39,360
We only want the extra stuff

877
00:38:39,360 --> 00:38:40,840
Not the play itself

878
00:38:40,840 --> 00:38:42,040
Then what are we even acting for?

879
00:38:42,040 --> 00:38:43,630
So we don't do the play?

880
00:38:43,630 --> 00:38:44,510
Why wouldn't we?

881
00:38:44,510 --> 00:38:46,510
No, no — didn't you want the extra parts?

882
00:38:46,510 --> 00:38:52,510
You didn't think we'd release the full play, did you?

883
00:38:52,510 --> 00:38:55,510
The edit mostly keeps just a bit of the play

884
00:38:55,510 --> 00:38:58,510
Then just the offstage stuff in between

885
00:38:58,510 --> 00:39:00,510
But you have to be in the play

886
00:39:00,510 --> 00:39:03,510
Right, like I said — the parts you acted

887
00:39:03,510 --> 00:39:04,510
How about this

888
00:39:04,510 --> 00:39:05,510
I actually think

889
00:39:05,510 --> 00:39:06,510
we can shorten it

890
00:39:06,510 --> 00:39:08,510
Yeah, just pick a few segments

891
00:39:08,510 --> 00:39:09,510
Don't run it start to finish

892
00:39:09,510 --> 00:39:10,510
There's no time

893
00:39:10,510 --> 00:39:11,510
Just pick a few segments

894
00:39:11,510 --> 00:39:16,510
Every actor gets one go

895
00:39:16,510 --> 00:39:19,510
Everyone's on camera once

896
00:39:19,510 --> 00:39:20,510
and says a few lines

897
00:39:20,510 --> 00:39:22,510
That way we get it all shot

898
00:39:22,510 --> 00:39:23,510
Us two

899
00:39:23,510 --> 00:39:24,510
How about it?

900
00:39:24,510 --> 00:39:26,510
Shoot the inside bits you think are classic

901
00:39:26,510 --> 00:39:28,510
Say you pick a few segments

902
00:39:28,510 --> 00:39:31,510
Maybe some that touch the play

903
00:39:31,510 --> 00:39:32,510
A bit from the play

904
00:39:32,510 --> 00:39:33,510
And some offstage stuff too

905
00:39:33,510 --> 00:39:34,510
What?

906
00:39:34,510 --> 00:39:35,510
All of it from the play

907
00:39:35,510 --> 00:39:36,510
Right?

908
00:39:36,510 --> 00:39:38,510
I want it all

909
00:39:38,510 --> 00:39:39,510
All of it

910
00:39:39,510 --> 00:39:40,510
All of it — keep going then

911
00:39:40,510 --> 00:39:48,270
Keep moving, fast — after we raced through rehearsal

912
00:39:49,440 --> 00:39:54,560
One at most, right? Come on — my car, my car

913
00:39:56,800 --> 00:40:01,080
Such a shame. If I lived like him, I'd...

914
00:40:01,080 --> 00:40:04,140
Alrighty

915
00:40:04,140 --> 00:40:06,970
Alrighty

916
00:40:06,970 --> 00:40:13,480
The audience is about this close

917
00:40:13,480 --> 00:40:16,180
The audience, this close

918
00:40:16,180 --> 00:40:18,180
The audience is just this close

919
00:40:18,180 --> 00:40:22,230
Right in my face

920
00:40:22,230 --> 00:40:24,230
In this perfunctory way

921
00:40:24,230 --> 00:40:26,230
No — what's the line?

922
00:40:26,230 --> 00:40:28,230
You threw me off my lines

923
00:40:28,230 --> 00:40:32,420
Sneaking around like this

924
00:40:32,420 --> 00:40:34,420
to build a relationship is an insult to love

925
00:40:34,420 --> 00:40:36,420
Constant run-ins

926
00:40:36,420 --> 00:40:38,420
a half-hearted confession

927
00:40:38,420 --> 00:40:41,500
even marrying over an accident

928
00:40:41,500 --> 00:40:44,860
just so the accident could be born

929
00:40:44,860 --> 00:40:46,500
He ought to be locked up

930
00:40:46,500 --> 00:40:47,830
I'm telling you

931
00:40:47,830 --> 00:40:50,390
But I'm not like him

932
00:40:50,390 --> 00:40:51,510
A thing like snitching —

933
00:40:51,510 --> 00:40:51,990
How are you any different?

934
00:40:51,990 --> 00:40:54,740
only someone like him would do it

935
00:40:54,740 --> 00:40:59,300
I can't stand people touching my shoulder

936
00:40:59,300 --> 00:41:02,570
It's over

937
00:41:02,570 --> 00:41:03,970
They're bullying me

938
00:41:05,570 --> 00:41:07,570
I can't stand people touching my shoulder

939
00:41:10,020 --> 00:41:11,420
Why isn't he back yet?

940
00:41:11,420 --> 00:41:14,460
Here he comes

941
00:41:14,460 --> 00:41:21,050
No idea

942
00:41:21,050 --> 00:41:21,850
Hey, you there

943
00:41:21,850 --> 00:41:23,040
You

944
00:41:23,040 --> 00:41:23,720
The Boss

945
00:41:23,720 --> 00:41:25,640
wants you to come by

946
00:41:25,640 --> 00:41:35,310
I'm off to see the Boss

947
00:41:35,310 --> 00:41:40,950
The script really has its logic problems

948
00:41:40,950 --> 00:41:43,550
Including some of the lines

949
00:41:43,550 --> 00:41:45,630
When I first got the script

950
00:41:45,630 --> 00:41:48,030
lots of lines made no sense to me

951
00:41:48,030 --> 00:41:55,670
Two, three days ago I still didn't get them

952
00:41:55,910 --> 00:41:57,110
What on earth did you mean by writing that?

953
00:41:57,820 --> 00:42:02,890
Then slowly you rationalize it to yourself

954
00:42:02,890 --> 00:42:06,090
and create from there

955
00:42:06,090 --> 00:42:16,290
Uh, I think us actors were all pretty serious

956
00:42:16,290 --> 00:42:19,900
Well then actually do it!

957
00:42:19,900 --> 00:42:33,520
Is he sick in the head here or what?

958
00:42:33,520 --> 00:42:39,810
Like, mentally ill?

959
00:42:39,810 --> 00:42:40,810
Not really

960
00:42:40,810 --> 00:42:42,810
But he's got a bit of it in him

961
00:42:42,810 --> 00:42:44,810
A guy like him

962
00:42:44,810 --> 00:42:49,980
Say he's 100% a menace to society

963
00:42:49,980 --> 00:42:52,050
that might be unfair to him

964
00:42:52,050 --> 00:42:55,050
But say 90% odds he'd do wrong

965
00:42:55,050 --> 00:42:58,060
that's definitely underselling it

966
00:42:58,060 --> 00:43:17,380
Two mics held up to you

967
00:43:17,380 --> 00:43:18,380
An interview

968
00:43:18,380 --> 00:43:19,380
Say something

969
00:43:19,380 --> 00:43:21,380
What a shit play

970
00:43:21,380 --> 00:43:26,200
Who the fuck wrote this

971
00:43:26,200 --> 00:43:30,660
I'd better not say

972
00:43:30,660 --> 00:43:35,260
Come say a few words

973
00:43:35,260 --> 00:43:36,260
The Boss is here

974
00:43:36,260 --> 00:43:37,260
My turn

975
00:43:37,260 --> 00:43:41,110
Hurry up

976
00:43:41,110 --> 00:43:42,110
Come on

977
00:43:42,110 --> 00:43:49,900
The Boss is here

978
00:43:49,900 --> 00:43:50,900
Let me introduce

979
00:43:50,900 --> 00:43:51,900
This is my Boss

980
00:43:51,900 --> 00:43:54,930
I'm his employee

981
00:43:54,930 --> 00:43:57,930
The exploited one

982
00:43:57,930 --> 00:43:59,930
Exploited how?

983
00:43:59,930 --> 00:44:01,930
I'd fucking love to know, exploited how

984
00:44:01,930 --> 00:44:04,340
Go on, tell me

985
00:44:04,340 --> 00:44:07,360
Right?

986
00:44:07,360 --> 00:44:08,360
I pay you

987
00:44:08,360 --> 00:44:10,360
Gave you a job, gave you money

988
00:44:10,360 --> 00:44:11,360
How did I exploit you?

989
00:44:11,360 --> 00:44:14,360
Don't you earn what you work for?

990
00:44:14,360 --> 00:44:15,360
Boss

991
00:44:15,360 --> 00:44:16,360
Exploited what?

992
00:44:16,360 --> 00:44:17,360
Right? Exploited what?

993
00:44:17,360 --> 00:44:18,360
Whining over nothing

994
00:44:18,360 --> 00:44:20,360
Yeah, whining over nothing

995
00:44:20,360 --> 00:44:23,360
Right? How have I ever exploited him?

996
00:44:23,360 --> 00:44:26,360
You get paid, don't you?

997
00:44:26,360 --> 00:44:28,360
Since you joined, how's he exploited you?

998
00:44:28,360 --> 00:44:30,360
You get paid? You have a job?

999
00:44:30,360 --> 00:44:31,360
How does that song go again?

1000
00:44:31,360 --> 00:44:32,360
What?

1001
00:44:32,360 --> 00:44:34,360
How does The Internationale go?

1002
00:44:34,360 --> 00:44:39,360
Arise, ye who refuse to be slaves

1003
00:44:39,360 --> 00:44:40,760
Don't dare sing that, really don't

1004
00:44:40,760 --> 00:44:41,560
Come on, from the top

1005
00:44:41,560 --> 00:44:45,160
Arise, ye who refuse to be slaves

1006
00:44:45,160 --> 00:44:46,560
Arise, ye hungry and cold

1007
00:44:46,560 --> 00:44:48,360
Arise, ye hungry and cold

1008
00:44:48,360 --> 00:44:49,560
I'll lead, you sing along

1009
00:44:49,560 --> 00:44:53,760
Arise, ye slaves of cold and hunger

1010
00:44:53,760 --> 00:44:57,760
Arise, ye wretched of the earth

1011
00:45:40,160 --> 00:45:41,760
Waiting for the slaughter

1012
00:45:41,760 --> 00:45:42,960
I even think

1013
00:45:42,960 --> 00:45:44,960
I'm worse off than a pig

1014
00:45:44,960 --> 00:45:46,560
A pig eats, then sleeps

1015
00:45:46,560 --> 00:45:48,360
sleeps, then eats, thinks of nothing

1016
00:45:48,360 --> 00:45:48,960
But me

1017
00:45:48,960 --> 00:45:51,760
me, I let myself be exploited

1018
00:45:53,760 --> 00:46:00,790
When I didn't know I was that pig

1019
00:46:00,790 --> 00:46:03,190
I ate just like the pigs

1020
00:46:03,190 --> 00:46:04,190
Slept

1021
00:46:04,190 --> 00:46:05,190
Worked

1022
00:46:05,190 --> 00:46:06,590
Thought about nothing

1023
00:46:06,590 --> 00:46:09,450
Once I know my final fate

1024
00:46:09,450 --> 00:46:11,250
I should fight back

1025
00:46:11,250 --> 00:46:12,900
No grand ideals

1026
00:46:12,900 --> 00:46:16,700
Rebel purely for my own interests

1027
00:46:16,700 --> 00:46:17,700
Oh

1028
00:46:17,700 --> 00:46:28,180
The blood in our chests is boiling

1029
00:46:28,180 --> 00:46:31,340
We will fight for the truth

1030
00:46:32,750 --> 00:46:35,750
Hi, I want to talk to these three

1031
00:46:35,750 --> 00:46:39,750
Smash the old world to smithereens

1032
00:46:39,750 --> 00:46:41,750
Just sing, it's fine

1033
00:46:41,750 --> 00:46:42,750
We did sing

1034
00:46:42,750 --> 00:46:44,750
I love Beijing's Tiananmen...

1035
00:46:44,750 --> 00:46:46,750
...where the sun rises

1036
00:46:50,980 --> 00:46:51,980
I hear

1037
00:46:51,980 --> 00:46:55,840
your attitude's been a bit off lately

1038
00:46:55,840 --> 00:46:58,840
Is something messing with your mood?

1039
00:46:58,840 --> 00:47:00,840
It's fine, just say it

1040
00:47:00,840 --> 00:47:03,840
I hope you'll accept my help

1041
00:47:03,840 --> 00:47:05,840
After all, you're new here

1042
00:47:05,840 --> 00:47:08,290
Fitting in takes some time

1043
00:47:08,290 --> 00:47:11,290
Save it. Cards on the table

1044
00:47:11,290 --> 00:47:15,990
You make us grind this rote work daily

1045
00:47:15,990 --> 00:47:18,990
till we can't think for ourselves

1046
00:47:18,990 --> 00:47:21,060
Work this endlessly repetitive

1047
00:47:21,060 --> 00:47:23,060
why not just let machines do it?

1048
00:47:23,060 --> 00:47:24,260
Nothing I can do about that

1049
00:47:24,260 --> 00:47:26,660
Machines can't do everything, can they?

1050
00:47:26,660 --> 00:47:27,660
Boss

1051
00:47:27,660 --> 00:47:29,860
I've been here since graduation

1052
00:47:29,860 --> 00:47:31,060
Why?

1053
00:47:31,060 --> 00:47:33,420
Because I think you can still be saved

1054
00:47:33,420 --> 00:47:36,420
Money has rotted all the others

1055
00:47:38,210 --> 00:47:39,610
Boss, you know what?

1056
00:47:39,610 --> 00:47:44,020
10% of people hold 90% of the resources

1057
00:47:44,020 --> 00:47:48,030
By the time it reaches us, just scraps

1058
00:47:48,030 --> 00:47:50,230
And you still make excuses for them

1059
00:47:50,230 --> 00:47:52,150
People have to eat, don't they?

1060
00:47:52,150 --> 00:47:53,180
Look

1061
00:47:53,180 --> 00:47:55,180
Back then you farmed for your grain

1062
00:47:55,180 --> 00:47:57,180
Now you're spared all that toil

1063
00:47:57,180 --> 00:48:00,410
Sacrifice a little dignity, eat your fill

1064
00:48:00,410 --> 00:48:02,570
Why won't you just bow your head?

1065
00:48:02,570 --> 00:48:04,570
Know why I can't fit in?

1066
00:48:04,570 --> 00:48:07,400
That crowd

1067
00:48:07,400 --> 00:48:11,400
hooked daily on bite-size cheap thrills

1068
00:48:11,400 --> 00:48:14,500
Off work, they dive into short videos

1069
00:48:14,500 --> 00:48:17,500
Hooked, feeding capitalists their traffic

1070
00:48:17,500 --> 00:48:21,350
Funnier still, they can't even

1071
00:48:21,350 --> 00:48:24,350
tell whether they're drowning in

1072
00:48:24,350 --> 00:48:31,830
They can't even see they're hooked on trash

1073
00:48:31,830 --> 00:48:34,430
I mean, if you've never tasted good food

1074
00:48:34,430 --> 00:48:37,550
you don't know your own food is swill

1075
00:48:37,550 --> 00:48:38,750
So what do you want?

1076
00:48:38,750 --> 00:48:39,950
If I were in your seat

1077
00:48:39,950 --> 00:48:42,350
I'd run a great purge

1078
00:48:42,350 --> 00:48:45,350
I'd screen an obscure art film in a meeting

1079
00:48:45,350 --> 00:48:48,750
Whoever pees, checks phones, or dozes off

1080
00:48:48,750 --> 00:48:49,950
Fire them all

1081
00:48:49,950 --> 00:48:51,550
Then I'd have no employees left

1082
00:48:51,550 --> 00:48:53,150
Look me in the eyes and say it

1083
00:48:53,150 --> 00:48:54,150
Understood

1084
00:48:54,150 --> 00:48:58,150
Look me in the eyes and say it. Hear me?

1085
00:48:58,150 --> 00:48:59,660
Understood

1086
00:48:59,660 --> 00:49:13,390
My eyes. Say it. Do you hear me?

1087
00:49:13,390 --> 00:49:15,810
I'm talking to you. Do you hear me?

1088
00:49:15,810 --> 00:49:18,810
I'm talking to you! Do you hear me?

1089
00:49:18,810 --> 00:49:22,450
I'm talking to you! Do you hear me?

1090
00:49:22,450 --> 00:49:28,700
I'm talking to you! Do you hear me?

1091
00:49:28,700 --> 00:49:30,700
Quit messing around

1092
00:49:30,700 --> 00:49:32,120
I hear you, I hear you

1093
00:49:32,120 --> 00:49:33,120
Sorry, Boss

1094
00:49:33,120 --> 00:49:36,120
What's going on with you lately?

1095
00:49:36,120 --> 00:49:39,120
Why the sour face every day?

1096
00:49:39,120 --> 00:49:41,120
I didn't do anything to you, did I?

1097
00:49:41,120 --> 00:49:44,270
They didn't either, right?

1098
00:49:44,270 --> 00:49:47,260
Say something!

1099
00:49:47,260 --> 00:49:49,260
Fine, don't talk then

1100
00:49:49,260 --> 00:49:51,420
You've been here a whole week

1101
00:49:51,420 --> 00:49:53,640
Say something!

1102
00:49:53,640 --> 00:49:55,640
And you still can't fit in with them

1103
00:49:55,640 --> 00:49:57,640
I'll take it to HR

1104
00:49:57,640 --> 00:49:59,640
Boss, I didn't mean it like that

1105
00:49:59,640 --> 00:50:02,640
It's the same mechanical work every day

1106
00:50:02,640 --> 00:50:04,640
It gets a bit boring

1107
00:50:04,640 --> 00:50:06,640
I feel like a machine

1108
00:50:06,640 --> 00:50:11,410
Might as well have a machine replace me

1109
00:50:11,410 --> 00:50:14,090
What a fucking great idea he's got

1110
00:50:14,090 --> 00:50:16,090
Then why not swap you for a machine?

1111
00:50:16,090 --> 00:50:17,050
What do I need you for?

1112
00:50:19,050 --> 00:50:20,370
You know why I hired you?

1113
00:50:21,770 --> 00:50:23,450
Because you're cheaper than a machine

1114
00:50:26,960 --> 00:50:29,160
I hired you fresh out of school

1115
00:50:29,160 --> 00:50:29,720
Why?

1116
00:50:32,590 --> 00:50:34,960
Because I thought you could still be saved

1117
00:50:34,960 --> 00:50:36,760
Most young people are way too cocky

1118
00:50:36,760 --> 00:50:39,580
All ambition, zero ability

1119
00:50:39,580 --> 00:50:41,900
You are the foundation of this society

1120
00:50:41,900 --> 00:50:43,420
If you lot won't take responsibility

1121
00:50:43,420 --> 00:50:45,980
this society will collapse

1122
00:50:45,980 --> 00:50:48,260
And you want to sink to their level?

1123
00:50:55,460 --> 00:50:58,380
You know why you can't fit in?

1124
00:50:58,380 --> 00:50:59,900
Look at them

1125
00:50:59,900 --> 00:51:02,220
Watching short videos all day

1126
00:51:02,220 --> 00:51:04,500
After work

1127
00:51:04,500 --> 00:51:07,590
they mess around with all kinds of junk

1128
00:51:07,590 --> 00:51:08,510
A little chat

1129
00:51:08,510 --> 00:51:09,670
a little tea

1130
00:51:09,670 --> 00:51:11,750
You must learn to fit into the collective

1131
00:51:11,750 --> 00:51:16,230
But I won't drown in this cheap entertainment

1132
00:51:16,230 --> 00:51:21,030
You haven't even looked, and it's "cheap"?

1133
00:51:21,030 --> 00:51:29,500
Just how noble are you?

1134
00:51:29,500 --> 00:51:31,220
Have him lay his cards on the table

1135
00:51:31,220 --> 00:51:32,060
Is he in or out?

1136
00:51:32,060 --> 00:51:35,380
Say something

1137
00:51:35,380 --> 00:51:36,500
Speak up!

1138
00:51:36,500 --> 00:51:39,140
Are you in or not?

1139
00:51:39,140 --> 00:51:43,180
I'm in

1140
00:51:43,180 --> 00:51:44,020
From now on, when you talk to me

1141
00:51:44,020 --> 00:51:45,300
look me in the eyes

1142
00:51:45,300 --> 00:51:46,980
Let me know you're talking to me

1143
00:51:46,980 --> 00:51:48,100
Understood?

1144
00:51:48,100 --> 00:51:48,980
Understood

1145
00:51:48,980 --> 00:51:50,850
Here it comes

1146
00:51:50,850 --> 00:51:51,690
Here

1147
00:51:51,690 --> 00:51:52,450
Thanks

1148
00:51:52,450 --> 00:51:54,280
Looking good

1149
00:51:54,280 --> 00:51:55,440
Almost didn't recognize you

1150
00:51:55,440 --> 00:51:57,820
Don't you bully him

1151
00:51:57,820 --> 00:51:59,820
If he acts up, hit him

1152
00:51:59,820 --> 00:52:01,820
I wouldn't dare

1153
00:52:01,820 --> 00:52:03,820
Playing twenty-somethings

1154
00:52:03,820 --> 00:52:05,820
for so many years now

1155
00:52:05,820 --> 00:52:07,820
I've picked up some bad habits

1156
00:52:07,820 --> 00:52:09,820
