01:03:58,320 --> 01:04:00,520
You know what happens if you grab me, right?

1442
01:04:00,520 --> 01:04:03,920
Worst case, I'll do last time all over again

1443
01:04:03,920 --> 01:04:06,320
I still don't know what happened last time

1444
01:04:06,320 --> 01:04:09,580
What happened last time?

1445
01:04:09,580 --> 01:04:11,180
Driving

1446
01:04:11,180 --> 01:04:12,780
Last time you were hauling a truckload

1447
01:04:12,780 --> 01:04:13,980
And he didn't want to go

1448
01:04:13,980 --> 01:04:14,780
But you made him go

1449
01:04:14,780 --> 01:04:15,980
He beat the guy up

1450
01:04:15,980 --> 01:04:18,180
Holy fuck

1451
01:04:18,180 --> 01:04:18,780
Really?

1452
01:04:18,780 --> 01:04:20,580
Forget it then

1453
01:04:20,580 --> 01:04:22,900
Let me tell you

1454
01:04:22,900 --> 01:04:24,940
I'll go get Lisa

1455
01:04:24,940 --> 01:04:26,620
Don't think you're such hot shit

1456
01:04:26,620 --> 01:04:30,510
With wigs on I can't even tell who you are

1457
01:04:30,510 --> 01:04:31,870
So tacky

1458
01:04:31,870 --> 01:04:32,830
Daughter

1459
01:04:32,830 --> 01:04:34,190
Don't let me see you again

1460
01:04:34,190 --> 01:04:39,610
Look at the state of you

1461
01:04:39,610 --> 01:04:40,810
Lisa

1462
01:04:40,810 --> 01:04:42,170
Daddy's here

1463
01:04:42,170 --> 01:04:45,010
Daddy

1464
01:04:45,010 --> 01:04:47,410
Wait, you're Lisa?

1465
01:04:47,410 --> 01:04:49,940
The moment it comes off

1466
01:04:49,940 --> 01:04:56,370
Turns out you're still you

1467
01:04:56,370 --> 01:04:58,010
Props! Is there even a props team?

1468
01:04:58,010 --> 01:04:59,530
No props at all

1469
01:04:59,530 --> 01:05:04,530
Miming now? Props? What a crew, seriously

1470
01:05:05,290 --> 01:05:06,930
Done acting, I'm pulling a diva

1471
01:05:06,930 --> 01:05:11,410
There is a result — Beifeng isn't like the usual theatre

1472
01:05:12,730 --> 01:05:15,530
The result is... the result is

1473
01:05:16,250 --> 01:05:19,530
The result is this thing has to pass the bar

1474
01:05:19,530 --> 01:05:22,250
But clearly we haven't gotten there yet

1475
01:05:22,250 --> 01:05:23,770
And we need to keep creating

1476
01:05:23,770 --> 01:05:26,730
Or my own character itself

1477
01:05:26,730 --> 01:05:29,850
Even two or three days before rehearsals

1478
01:05:29,850 --> 01:05:32,530
We were still finding the hooker character

1479
01:05:32,530 --> 01:05:33,690
We were still discussing

1480
01:05:33,690 --> 01:05:35,490
Still searching inside the character

1481
01:05:35,490 --> 01:05:37,130
Searching right up until tonight's stage

1482
01:05:37,130 --> 01:05:38,610
But I think it's still not enough

1483
01:05:38,610 --> 01:05:40,850
We have to keep searching

1484
01:05:40,850 --> 01:05:43,930
My part alone is three roles

1485
01:05:43,930 --> 01:05:45,090
Right from the entrance

1486
01:05:45,090 --> 01:05:47,850
It's the Robber forcing his way in

1487
01:05:47,850 --> 01:05:49,530
And a hostage, that state

1488
01:05:49,530 --> 01:05:51,050
So I think

1489
01:05:51,050 --> 01:05:53,290
Everyone needs more time

1490
01:05:53,290 --> 01:05:54,170
To create together

1491
01:05:54,170 --> 01:05:55,370
To find our groove together

1492
01:05:55,370 --> 01:05:57,050
The result matters too

1493
01:05:57,050 --> 01:06:00,170
But the most important meaning, I think

1494
01:06:00,170 --> 01:06:03,770
This play existing means a lot to Beifeng

1495
01:06:03,770 --> 01:06:06,410
Beifeng truly exists now, it's real

1496
01:06:06,890 --> 01:06:09,850
So really, thank you, thank you

1497
01:06:11,720 --> 01:06:13,160
There's one thing I find interesting

1498
01:06:13,160 --> 01:06:18,200
Like three actors all said they never found

1499
01:06:18,840 --> 01:06:19,640
That spot

1500
01:06:19,640 --> 01:06:22,040
I don't know how Beifeng defines that now

1501
01:06:22,040 --> 01:06:26,440
Instead of searching or talking about finding it

1502
01:06:26,520 --> 01:06:28,520
Just go try being that person

1503
01:06:28,520 --> 01:06:29,520
Or rather

1504
01:06:29,520 --> 01:06:30,520
Just because

1505
01:06:30,520 --> 01:06:32,520
I mean, right now Beifeng is still

1506
01:06:32,520 --> 01:06:33,520
Like

1507
01:06:33,520 --> 01:06:34,520
It's still

1508
01:06:34,520 --> 01:06:36,520
So-called play-acting

1509
01:06:36,520 --> 01:06:37,520
I mean

1510
01:06:37,520 --> 01:06:38,520
That is, or rather

1511
01:06:38,520 --> 01:06:40,520
You can leap right into it

1512
01:06:40,520 --> 01:06:41,520
And I really didn't like the playwright's

1513
01:06:41,520 --> 01:06:43,520
Opening line just now

1514
01:06:43,520 --> 01:06:45,520
Saying we made a lot of mistakes

1515
01:06:45,520 --> 01:06:46,520
Like the lighting problems

1516
01:06:46,520 --> 01:06:47,520
That, uh

1517
01:06:47,520 --> 01:06:48,520
The transitions were bad

1518
01:06:48,520 --> 01:06:49,520
Well, for example

1519
01:06:49,520 --> 01:06:50,520
Right

1520
01:06:50,520 --> 01:06:51,520
One, in itself

1521
01:06:51,520 --> 01:06:52,520
Take film, for example

1522
01:06:52,520 --> 01:06:53,520
Sound comes in first too

1523
01:06:53,520 --> 01:06:54,520
Then the picture opens

1524
01:06:54,520 --> 01:06:56,320
Or some jump-cut techniques

1525
01:06:56,320 --> 01:06:57,160
That's all totally normal

1526
01:06:57,160 --> 01:06:59,920
There's no fixed standard template

1527
01:06:59,920 --> 01:07:00,520
And then

1528
01:07:00,520 --> 01:07:02,120
My way is just fine

1529
01:07:02,120 --> 01:07:03,320
The way I played it

1530
01:07:03,320 --> 01:07:03,720
Right

1531
01:07:03,720 --> 01:07:05,320
I played it wrong

1532
01:07:05,320 --> 01:07:07,920
Or you think your way of playing it is right

1533
01:07:07,920 --> 01:07:10,320
Then who gave you that template of legitimacy?

1534
01:07:10,320 --> 01:07:11,920
Me, myself

1535
01:07:11,920 --> 01:07:12,920
Myself

1536
01:07:12,920 --> 01:07:14,720
I myself think I played it wrong

1537
01:07:17,220 --> 01:07:19,890
He seems to have some kind of glow

1538
01:07:19,890 --> 01:07:22,210
Warm and pure

1539
01:07:22,210 --> 01:07:23,810
He was meant to be pure

1540
01:07:23,810 --> 01:07:26,010
He doesn't belong on this filthy street

1541
01:07:26,010 --> 01:07:28,650
Shouldn't be in my sight

1542
01:07:28,650 --> 01:07:31,210
He shouldn't be doing this kind of work

1543
01:07:31,210 --> 01:07:33,490
If he weren't here, he'd be a star

1544
01:07:33,490 --> 01:07:36,610
He should be smiling at flashbulbs on a red carpet

1545
01:07:36,610 --> 01:07:43,540
But now no one cherishes his smile

1546
01:07:43,540 --> 01:07:47,470
I wish a real rain would wash this street clean

1547
01:07:47,470 --> 01:07:49,660
Or one day

1548
01:07:49,660 --> 01:07:52,500
When they all gather

1549
01:07:52,500 --> 01:07:53,960
I mean

1550
01:07:53,960 --> 01:07:56,820
Everyone packed together out on the street

1551
01:07:56,820 --> 01:07:59,670
I'll drive a cement truck

1552
01:07:59,670 --> 01:08:02,860
And crush them all to death

1553
01:08:02,860 --> 01:08:04,460
Twice

1554
01:08:04,460 --> 01:08:06,000
Three times

1555
01:08:06,000 --> 01:08:09,450
Till their bones are mashed together

1556
01:08:09,450 --> 01:08:14,160
Till the screaming stops for good

1557
01:08:14,160 --> 01:08:16,490
God, I'd love to do that

1558
01:08:16,490 --> 01:08:19,040
I might need a piece

1559
01:08:19,040 --> 01:08:20,440
For when I run into them

1560
01:08:20,440 --> 01:08:21,640
I can do it

1561
01:08:39,620 --> 01:08:42,780
Sleep now, my beloved

1562
01:08:42,780 --> 01:08:44,060
This is where you rave too, right?

1563
01:08:44,060 --> 01:08:48,380
Sleep, sleep

1564
01:08:48,380 --> 01:08:52,580
Lao Song

1565
01:08:52,580 --> 01:08:53,580
laughing over here

1566
01:08:53,580 --> 01:08:55,560
Shh

1567
01:08:55,560 --> 01:09:02,730
No, I mean, we're on stage here

1568
01:09:02,730 --> 01:09:03,530
Once he's asleep

1569
01:09:03,530 --> 01:09:04,810
he even sleeps with flair

1570
01:09:04,810 --> 01:09:07,890
Sleep

1571
01:09:07,890 --> 01:09:09,490
Hurry up and sleep

1572
01:09:09,490 --> 01:09:10,770
I'm sleeping

1573
01:09:10,770 --> 01:09:16,110
Your chest can't hold a bed

1574
01:09:16,110 --> 01:09:18,190
Hurry up and fall asleep

1575
01:09:18,190 --> 01:09:23,640
You've lost track of the night

1576
01:09:23,640 --> 01:09:26,800
Nice

1577
01:09:26,800 --> 01:09:28,200
No more sorrow

1578
01:09:28,200 --> 01:09:30,040
No more hunger

1579
01:09:30,040 --> 01:09:38,870
No more empty meal tickets

1580
01:09:38,870 --> 01:09:41,380
You'll hit the jackpot

1581
01:09:41,380 --> 01:09:43,780
Hurry up and fall asleep

1582
01:09:43,780 --> 01:09:46,790
The ones you love will remember

1583
01:09:46,790 --> 01:09:48,710
Bravo, what a poem

1584
01:09:48,710 --> 01:09:49,710
Bravo

1585
01:09:49,710 --> 01:09:50,990
Li Bai wrote that, right?

1586
01:09:50,990 --> 01:09:52,350
Hurry up and sleep

1587
01:09:52,350 --> 01:09:53,890
Never mind what the heart wants

1588
01:09:53,890 --> 01:09:56,940
Hurry up and fall asleep

1589
01:09:56,940 --> 01:10:00,460
No need to wallow in self-pity

1590
01:10:00,460 --> 01:10:03,660
Hurry up and fall asleep

1591
01:10:03,660 --> 01:10:07,790
The dream within the dream

1592
01:10:07,790 --> 01:10:11,050
can learn the creativity of our world

1593
01:10:11,050 --> 01:10:14,850
can go back to before it went wrong

1594
01:10:14,850 --> 01:10:18,430
back into the amniotic fluid, back

1595
01:10:18,430 --> 01:10:19,870
to before conception

1596
01:10:22,230 --> 01:10:23,230
Great show, great show

1597
01:10:26,230 --> 01:10:27,230
Someone

1598
01:10:27,230 --> 01:10:29,230
Someone wants to cover our eyes

1599
01:10:29,230 --> 01:10:30,230
gag our mouths

1600
01:10:30,230 --> 01:10:32,230
pin down our hands

1601
01:10:32,230 --> 01:10:34,230
pretend all is normal, nothing happened

1602
01:10:34,230 --> 01:10:36,230
I've seen it

1603
01:10:36,230 --> 01:10:39,360
I know what this place was like when he fled

1604
01:10:39,360 --> 01:10:41,360
Now look what you've turned it into

1605
01:10:41,360 --> 01:10:42,360
He's down

1606
01:10:48,740 --> 01:10:49,740
My back's given out

1607
01:10:51,970 --> 01:10:58,320
Call an ambulance, I can't move

1608
01:10:58,320 --> 01:11:04,860
Which act are we on?

1609
01:11:04,860 --> 01:11:05,860
That's it?

1610
01:11:05,860 --> 01:11:06,860
That's it?

1611
01:11:06,860 --> 01:11:07,860
Nope

1612
01:11:07,860 --> 01:11:16,030
The part where the Boss gets shot

1613
01:11:16,030 --> 01:11:18,030
No, no, no

1614
01:11:18,030 --> 01:11:20,030
My bit

1615
01:11:20,030 --> 01:11:22,030
Ugh, this is so annoying

1616
01:11:22,030 --> 01:11:23,030
Is there more?

1617
01:11:23,030 --> 01:11:24,030
Mine, mine

1618
01:11:24,030 --> 01:11:53,320
Who made the rules?

1619
01:11:53,320 --> 01:11:57,120
Those who profit sit closest to the rules

1620
01:11:57,220 --> 01:12:00,670
This must be just what they wanted

1621
01:12:00,770 --> 01:12:01,570
And they succeeded

1622
01:12:01,670 --> 01:12:04,460
They cut people like me out of society

1623
01:12:04,560 --> 01:12:06,800
I should head back

1624
01:12:06,900 --> 01:12:09,810
This is my return ticket

1625
01:12:09,910 --> 01:12:13,560
I mean, we all rejoin society someday

1626
01:12:13,660 --> 01:12:17,020
Either buy a few friends with money

1627
01:12:17,120 --> 01:12:20,910
or make a few enemies with brute force

1628
01:12:21,010 --> 01:12:29,110
I just checked my bank balance

1629
01:12:29,210 --> 01:12:32,110
Enough to last a lifetime if I never work

1630
01:12:32,110 --> 01:12:34,110
But there's one condition

1631
01:12:34,110 --> 01:12:36,110
I'd have to die tomorrow

1632
01:12:36,110 --> 01:12:38,780
Not one day more

1633
01:12:38,780 --> 01:12:40,780
Ring ring. The phone's ringing

1634
01:12:40,780 --> 01:12:44,350
The poor can't afford one of these

1635
01:12:44,350 --> 01:12:50,190
Hello?

1636
01:12:50,190 --> 01:12:52,900
Listen, I've got no money to pay you back

1637
01:12:52,900 --> 01:12:55,470
Worst case, come kill me

1638
01:12:55,470 --> 01:12:57,600
Or I'll jump off this building

1639
01:12:57,600 --> 01:13:02,640
Happy now?

1640
01:13:02,640 --> 01:13:04,830
He swore at me

1641
01:13:11,730 --> 01:13:15,730
So much in this world I've yet to try

1642
01:13:15,730 --> 01:13:18,690
I do this today, that tomorrow

1643
01:13:18,690 --> 01:13:21,770
In my heart, what makes me happy is right

1644
01:13:21,770 --> 01:13:23,810
What I loathe becomes wrong. And yet

1645
01:13:23,810 --> 01:13:27,250
people keep telling me my joys are wrong

1646
01:13:27,250 --> 01:13:31,290
I can't tell anymore, it's all displaced

1647
01:13:31,290 --> 01:13:40,300
Someone has to stand up

1648
01:13:40,300 --> 01:13:44,100
Even just not joining their filth counts

1649
01:13:44,100 --> 01:13:47,830
No sound effect

1650
01:13:47,830 --> 01:14:06,540
I just won't live penned up like a pig

1651
01:14:06,540 --> 01:14:08,340
waiting to be slaughtered

1652
01:14:08,340 --> 01:14:11,340
I'm not even as good as a pig

1653
01:14:11,340 --> 01:14:13,340
A pig eats, sleeps, eats

1654
01:14:13,340 --> 01:14:14,340
never has to think

1655
01:14:14,340 --> 01:14:18,340
And me? I just finished my PhD

1656
01:14:18,340 --> 01:14:22,240
Before I knew which pig I was

1657
01:14:22,240 --> 01:14:24,240
I could live like a pig

1658
01:14:24,240 --> 01:14:26,240
eat, sleep, work

1659
01:14:26,240 --> 01:14:28,240
think about nothing

1660
01:14:28,240 --> 01:14:31,240
But all I know is my final fate

1661
01:14:31,240 --> 01:14:33,240
so I have to fight back

1662
01:14:33,240 --> 01:14:35,240
Not for some ideal

1663
01:14:35,240 --> 01:14:37,690
just purely

1664
01:14:37,690 --> 01:15:15,340
fighting for my own interests

1665
01:15:25,110 --> 01:15:54,940
How do we shout it?

1666
01:15:54,940 --> 01:16:25,780
Is this me?

1667
01:16:25,780 --> 01:16:27,780
This must be who I was meant to become

1668
01:16:27,780 --> 01:16:31,090
They call this

1669
01:16:31,540 --> 01:16:34,140
the birth pangs of the times

1670
01:16:34,140 --> 01:16:36,140
a necessary sacrifice

1671
01:16:36,140 --> 01:16:43,220
the road that must be walked

1672
01:16:43,220 --> 01:16:44,220
Why is he stripping?

1673
01:16:44,220 --> 01:16:45,220
Isn't this the last act?

1674
01:16:45,220 --> 01:16:47,640
But my whole life...

1675
01:16:47,640 --> 01:16:48,640
He stripped once midway too

1676
01:16:48,640 --> 01:16:50,500
who would even know

1677
01:16:50,500 --> 01:16:52,500
Call it publicity, a selling point

1678
01:16:52,500 --> 01:16:53,500
That's called exhibitionism

1679
01:16:53,500 --> 01:16:54,460
So where were we?

1680
01:16:54,460 --> 01:16:55,100
Right?

1681
01:16:55,100 --> 01:17:07,180
Where'd the feelings get to?

1682
01:17:07,180 --> 01:17:08,060
Come on, next scene

1683
01:17:08,060 --> 01:17:08,940
Where were we?

1684
01:17:08,940 --> 01:17:23,410
I didn't sell it

1685
01:17:23,410 --> 01:17:24,450
Sealed off

1686
01:17:28,050 --> 01:17:29,130
The Big One is coming

1687
01:17:29,130 --> 01:17:30,370
The Big One is coming

1688
01:17:30,370 --> 01:17:31,610
No, no, the big-big one

1689
01:17:31,610 --> 01:17:33,090
This is Act Six already, right?

1690
01:17:33,090 --> 01:17:34,410
The Big One comes later, right?

1691
01:17:34,410 --> 01:17:35,090
Where are we?

1692
01:17:35,090 --> 01:17:35,930
Act Six, I think

1693
01:17:35,930 --> 01:17:36,650
Act Six

1694
01:17:36,650 --> 01:17:36,930
Yeah

1695
01:17:36,930 --> 01:17:38,130
Give it to me

1696
01:17:38,130 --> 01:17:39,210
Still mine

1697
01:17:52,970 --> 01:17:55,060
Honestly speaking

1698
01:17:55,060 --> 01:17:56,500
I still hope this time of ours

1699
01:17:56,500 --> 01:18:00,620
won't be the last

1700
01:18:00,620 --> 01:18:02,860
I've figured it out

1701
01:18:02,860 --> 01:18:04,860
Big dreams, weak hands—it got to me

1702
01:18:04,860 --> 01:18:10,460
The road you chose, you walk step by step

1703
01:18:10,460 --> 01:18:13,850
Why didn't you show this attitude sooner?

1704
01:18:13,850 --> 01:18:16,010
They all got raises this month

1705
01:18:16,010 --> 01:18:17,010
All except you

1706
01:18:17,010 --> 01:18:19,040
Because of your attitude problem

1707
01:18:19,040 --> 01:18:20,040
I didn't give you one

1708
01:18:20,040 --> 01:18:24,830
But my numbers match theirs this month

1709
01:18:24,830 --> 01:18:28,280
So why, at the last second,

1710
01:18:28,280 --> 01:18:30,280
do you dock my wages?

1711
01:18:30,280 --> 01:18:32,280
I'm not docking your wages

1712
01:18:32,280 --> 01:18:35,980
You're just not one with the collective yet

1713
01:18:35,980 --> 01:18:37,980
So no raise for you this month

1714
01:18:37,980 --> 01:18:41,810
My point is to make you see

1715
01:18:41,810 --> 01:18:44,100
numbers don't come first

1716
01:18:44,100 --> 01:18:46,100
Attitude is what matters most

1717
01:18:46,100 --> 01:18:49,440
Once you're sitting where I sit

1718
01:18:49,440 --> 01:18:50,440
you'll understand

1719
01:18:50,440 --> 01:18:53,440
When your company runs like a machine

1720
01:18:53,440 --> 01:18:55,630
the last thing you want to see

1721
01:18:55,630 --> 01:18:57,630
is one of the gears

1722
01:18:57,630 --> 01:18:59,890
turning the wrong way

1723
01:18:59,890 --> 01:19:02,020
