Didn't think you'd keep yours either

2298
01:45:38,230 --> 01:45:40,430
Been a little disappointed lately

2299
01:45:40,430 --> 01:45:42,950
I didn't become who I wanted to be

2300
01:45:42,950 --> 01:45:44,830
And I shut myself away

2301
01:45:44,830 --> 01:45:45,910
You've pulled this one before

2302
01:45:45,910 --> 01:45:48,780
I don't have many friends, you know

2303
01:45:48,780 --> 01:45:51,510
No, you know I told you before

2304
01:45:51,510 --> 01:45:54,430
Then you simply forgot

2305
01:45:54,430 --> 01:45:56,510
Laugh at me if you want

2306
01:45:56,510 --> 01:46:00,880
You're the one closest to my heart

2307
01:46:00,880 --> 01:46:03,400
See, you're still laughing at me

2308
01:46:03,400 --> 01:46:04,800
So be it

2309
01:46:04,800 --> 01:46:08,960
Like anyone truly knows another's heart

2310
01:46:08,960 --> 01:46:11,560
There's so much I want to tell you

2311
01:46:11,560 --> 01:46:13,160
I used to gripe you never let me take it back

2312
01:46:13,160 --> 01:46:14,880
I used to gripe you'd never take it back

2313
01:46:14,880 --> 01:46:16,800
Now I understand

2314
01:46:16,800 --> 01:46:18,320
I always used to complain

2315
01:46:18,320 --> 01:46:19,800
You wouldn't let me take it back

2316
01:46:19,800 --> 01:46:21,240
Wouldn't give me the time of day

2317
01:46:21,240 --> 01:46:23,200
Now I understand

2318
01:46:23,200 --> 01:46:24,160
I regret it

2319
01:46:24,160 --> 01:46:25,880
If your boyfriend asks who called

2320
01:46:25,880 --> 01:46:27,320
You won't get it tomorrow afternoon

2321
01:46:27,320 --> 01:46:28,680
I'll talk to him

2322
01:46:28,680 --> 01:46:30,440
Won't get it tomorrow afternoon

2323
01:46:30,440 --> 01:46:31,920
What is this?

2324
01:46:31,920 --> 01:46:34,720
If your boyfriend asks who called

2325
01:46:34,720 --> 01:46:40,000
Hand him the phone, I'll talk to him

2326
01:46:40,000 --> 01:46:42,380
Beep, beep

2327
01:46:42,380 --> 01:46:45,740
A busy tone came from the other end

2328
01:46:45,740 --> 01:46:47,540
The higher-ups treat me alright

2329
01:46:47,540 --> 01:46:49,900
The higher-ups treat me alright

2330
01:46:49,900 --> 01:46:51,940
Said they'd hold my position for me

2331
01:46:51,940 --> 01:46:54,580
Told me to stay home and clear my head

2332
01:46:54,580 --> 01:46:56,740
And come back once I've figured it out

2333
01:46:56,740 --> 01:46:59,300
He said, the day I finally figure it out

2334
01:46:59,300 --> 01:47:01,780
He'll give me a call

2335
01:47:01,780 --> 01:47:04,060
And forget about making headlines

2336
01:47:04,060 --> 01:47:07,020
I don't think I'll ever make it big

2337
01:47:07,020 --> 01:47:11,020
My name will never appear on TV

2338
01:47:11,020 --> 01:47:16,020
Those interview lines and speeches are useless now

2339
01:47:16,020 --> 01:47:18,020
I want to be a sociologist

2340
01:47:18,020 --> 01:47:21,020
So my thinking can be put to use

2341
01:47:21,020 --> 01:47:29,750
I don't want my job to be mindless repetition

2342
01:47:29,750 --> 01:47:33,940
Didn't I drop ash during the scene just now?

2343
01:47:33,940 --> 01:47:36,940
I did so much, yet it's like nothing happened

2344
01:47:36,940 --> 01:47:39,940
Back to the same jobless drifting days

2345
01:47:39,940 --> 01:47:42,940
And what even is this feeling?

2346
01:47:42,940 --> 01:47:45,940
The Boss keeps on sucking up capital

2347
01:47:45,940 --> 01:47:48,940
That smug look on his face

2348
01:47:48,940 --> 01:47:51,940
Even his white shirt disgusts me

2349
01:47:51,940 --> 01:47:54,070
If the justice I fought to uphold

2350
01:47:54,070 --> 01:47:57,070
And the truth I chased all turn to nothing

2351
01:47:57,070 --> 01:48:01,070
Then what in this world can ever change?

2352
01:48:01,070 --> 01:48:49,680
Got a light?

2353
01:48:49,680 --> 01:48:57,660
How did you find my place?

2354
01:48:57,660 --> 01:49:04,660
I thought no one could find me

2355
01:49:04,660 --> 01:49:07,660
It's so quiet in the hallway

2356
01:49:07,660 --> 01:49:11,880
I don't want anyone disturbing me

2357
01:49:11,880 --> 01:49:16,880
I came to catch up with you

2358
01:49:16,880 --> 01:49:18,880
If you mind

2359
01:49:18,880 --> 01:49:22,390
I can leave right now

2360
01:49:22,390 --> 01:49:25,390
We've met twice, what's to catch up on?

2361
01:49:25,390 --> 01:49:29,390
Maybe once isn't enough to know each other

2362
01:49:29,390 --> 01:49:33,390
But by the third time, nothing's off-limits

2363
01:49:33,390 --> 01:49:39,390
I like letting boys know me through my body

2364
01:49:39,390 --> 01:49:42,900
Is that how you treat your clients too?

2365
01:49:42,900 --> 01:49:45,900
If this is one of your services, you can go

2366
01:49:45,900 --> 01:49:48,900
We never actually made a deal

2367
01:49:48,900 --> 01:49:50,900
You can go home now

2368
01:49:50,900 --> 01:49:56,060
So you're still a virgin

2369
01:49:56,060 --> 01:50:00,060
I don't like love made in bed

2370
01:50:00,060 --> 01:50:03,060
Is lust really the answer to love?

2371
01:50:03,060 --> 01:50:06,060
But I have done it before

2372
01:50:06,060 --> 01:50:11,060
If you're trying to mock me with that

2373
01:50:11,060 --> 01:50:16,670
Just go

2374
01:50:16,670 --> 01:50:20,660
Will you leave with me?

2375
01:50:20,660 --> 01:50:28,690
So you're leaving this place

2376
01:50:28,910 --> 01:50:29,870
You're right

2377
01:50:29,870 --> 01:50:35,400
I mean you're tired of the way you live

2378
01:50:35,400 --> 01:50:36,920
You're right

2379
01:50:36,920 --> 01:50:41,660
Maybe I've had enough of cheap love

2380
01:50:41,660 --> 01:50:44,570
And of being used as an outlet

2381
01:50:44,570 --> 01:50:48,100
Maybe you've fulfilled your ideal here

2382
01:50:48,100 --> 01:50:50,360
Even giving it up doesn't matter

2383
01:50:50,360 --> 01:50:52,650
As long as you want to leave

2384
01:50:52,650 --> 01:50:55,160
I hope you'll come away with me

2385
01:50:55,160 --> 01:51:05,100
I... I still have things to settle

2386
01:51:05,100 --> 01:51:08,780
A man either dies where his ideal ends

2387
01:51:08,780 --> 01:51:12,630
Or dies on the road to reaching it

2388
01:51:12,630 --> 01:51:16,140
You're a romantic

2389
01:51:16,140 --> 01:51:18,120
No, I hate Romanticism

2390
01:51:18,120 --> 01:51:20,840
They think feelings alone solve problems

2391
01:51:20,840 --> 01:51:22,040
I'm not like that

2392
01:51:22,040 --> 01:51:25,560
I pursue the absolute truth of this world

2393
01:51:25,560 --> 01:51:28,340
And I wish everyone were like me

2394
01:51:28,340 --> 01:51:31,190
Seeing how false this world is

2395
01:51:31,190 --> 01:51:34,930
But they should discover the truth themselves

2396
01:51:34,930 --> 01:51:37,410
Only then do their lives have meaning

2397
01:51:37,410 --> 01:51:39,810
Let them expose the lies themselves

2398
01:51:39,810 --> 01:51:42,170
Then fight and cry out for the truth

2399
01:51:42,170 --> 01:51:45,820
Instead of coldly looking on

2400
01:51:45,820 --> 01:51:46,700
You're right

2401
01:51:46,700 --> 01:51:50,790
Except you're a realist

2402
01:51:50,790 --> 01:51:52,710
If escaping reality

2403
01:51:52,710 --> 01:51:54,670
Is what you call idealism

2404
01:51:54,670 --> 01:51:59,850
Then where will you go?

2405
01:51:59,850 --> 01:52:05,250
I am a lone island

2406
01:52:05,250 --> 01:52:08,330
Where does the ocean flow?

2407
01:52:08,330 --> 01:52:10,980
What?

2408
01:52:10,980 --> 01:52:15,070
There's an unclaimed little house in the country

2409
01:52:15,070 --> 01:52:17,150
And an abandoned field

2410
01:52:17,150 --> 01:52:23,310
I'd live with a man who treats me as his whole world

2411
01:52:23,310 --> 01:52:32,860
I need to put myself back together

2412
01:52:32,860 --> 01:52:35,020
Will you wait for me?

2413
01:52:35,020 --> 01:52:46,630
Did I ever say that?

2414
01:52:46,630 --> 01:52:49,410
Is that you?

2415
01:52:49,410 --> 01:53:13,370
Sorry — broke character laughing

2416
01:53:13,370 --> 01:53:16,580
What are you laughing at?

2417
01:53:16,580 --> 01:53:20,660
This scene is too long

2418
01:53:20,660 --> 01:53:21,580
It's good, it's good

2419
01:53:21,580 --> 01:53:22,700
You did say it

2420
01:53:22,700 --> 01:53:25,540
Is that you?

2421
01:53:25,540 --> 01:53:29,030
Cut this scene

2422
01:53:29,030 --> 01:53:31,510
Right, this scene can't leave this room

2423
01:53:31,510 --> 01:53:33,710
If it leaks, the price goes up

2424
01:53:33,710 --> 01:53:36,660
So which part next?

2425
01:53:36,660 --> 01:53:42,150
Oh, my turn — the police partners

2426
01:53:42,150 --> 01:53:43,180
Go on

2427
01:53:43,180 --> 01:53:44,180
Okay

2428
01:53:44,180 --> 01:53:52,940
Hey, what's wrong?

2429
01:53:52,940 --> 01:53:55,930
Why did the mood suddenly get heavy?

2430
01:53:55,930 --> 01:53:58,500
Come on

2431
01:53:58,500 --> 01:54:12,550
What time is it?

2432
01:54:12,550 --> 01:54:14,470
Ten past ten

2433
01:54:14,470 --> 01:54:16,620
So this case is closed

2434
01:54:16,620 --> 01:54:18,620
Remember to get me the report

2435
01:54:18,620 --> 01:54:22,970
All for this gun

2436
01:54:22,970 --> 01:54:24,650
Sorry to drag you out here

2437
01:54:24,650 --> 01:54:26,780
Is that kid really possessed?

2438
01:54:26,780 --> 01:54:28,780
He's pretty normal

2439
01:54:28,780 --> 01:54:30,780
It's just that nobody else is an idealist

2440
01:54:30,780 --> 01:54:32,780
That's what makes him look ridiculous

2441
01:54:32,780 --> 01:54:35,060
He reminds me of you

2442
01:54:35,060 --> 01:54:37,830
Me?

2443
01:54:37,830 --> 01:54:40,090
I'm nothing like him

2444
01:54:40,090 --> 01:54:42,090
My door doesn't have that many locks

2445
01:54:42,090 --> 01:54:44,090
And I only have two keys

2446
01:54:44,090 --> 01:54:46,090
One of them is still with you

2447
01:54:46,090 --> 01:54:50,010
That time you finally came over

2448
01:54:50,010 --> 01:54:53,030
I opened the door

2449
01:54:53,030 --> 01:54:55,220
Walked into the bedroom

2450
01:54:55,220 --> 01:54:57,960
And there you were with your chick

2451
01:54:57,960 --> 01:55:01,080
Just standing on the bed

2452
01:55:01,080 --> 01:55:08,330
I wanted to gouge my own eyes out

2453
01:55:08,330 --> 01:55:09,330
Anyway

2454
01:55:09,330 --> 01:55:11,390
We shouldn't have dragged the audience into this

2455
01:55:11,390 --> 01:55:12,390
Even if we investigate him

2456
01:55:12,390 --> 01:55:13,390
It should wait until the operation is over

2457
01:55:13,390 --> 01:55:19,040
Your first year on the force

2458
01:55:19,040 --> 01:55:21,420
Your uniform was covered in snot

2459
01:55:21,420 --> 01:55:24,030
You were a greenhorn

2460
01:55:25,930 --> 01:55:27,120
Yes

2461
01:55:27,120 --> 01:55:29,120
The bureau was a mess back then

2462
01:55:29,120 --> 01:55:30,120
If the chief hadn't gone down

2463
01:55:30,120 --> 01:55:32,280
Who knows how it would've ended

2464
01:55:32,280 --> 01:55:34,280
In the end it was you who reported him

2465
01:55:34,280 --> 01:55:36,280
That's how you made squad leader

2466
01:55:36,280 --> 01:55:38,280
And waded into this muddy water of yours

2467
01:55:38,280 --> 01:55:39,280
That's right

2468
01:55:39,280 --> 01:55:41,280
If it were her

2469
01:55:41,280 --> 01:55:43,280
She would never have done that

2470
01:55:43,280 --> 01:55:45,660
She'd stand at the prosecutor's gate

2471
01:55:45,660 --> 01:55:48,660
Soaking the files with the sweat of her hands

2472
01:55:48,660 --> 01:55:50,660
And then turn around and go home

2473
01:55:50,660 --> 01:55:52,300
And what does that tell you?

2474
01:55:52,300 --> 01:55:55,690
You both want to protect something

2475
01:55:55,690 --> 01:55:58,690
Whether your own interests or justice

2476
01:55:58,690 --> 01:56:00,690
You're a doer

2477
01:56:00,690 --> 01:56:01,690
You act first

2478
01:56:01,690 --> 01:56:05,650
She thinks first

2479
01:56:05,650 --> 01:56:09,100
You're mocking me for being reckless

2480
01:56:09,100 --> 01:56:11,100
I can hear it

2481
01:56:11,100 --> 01:56:13,610
You grew up in a stable family

2482
01:56:13,610 --> 01:56:15,610
Went to the police academy

2483
01:56:15,610 --> 01:56:17,610
Elite of the elite

2484
01:56:17,610 --> 01:56:20,020
While he's like a rat

2485
01:56:20,020 --> 01:56:22,020
Living in the sewer

2486
01:56:22,020 --> 01:56:23,020
So terrified by the vast sewage system

2487
01:56:23,020 --> 01:56:25,020
He can't climb out

2488
01:56:25,020 --> 01:56:27,060
Still cursing

2489
01:56:27,060 --> 01:56:29,060
Which bastard dug this thing so deep

2490
01:56:29,060 --> 01:56:31,470
That's him

2491
01:56:31,470 --> 01:56:35,660
He doesn't deserve to see this world

2492
01:56:35,660 --> 01:56:39,970
Then does he count as human?

2493
01:56:39,970 --> 01:56:47,500
Put tonight on my tab

2494
01:56:47,500 --> 01:56:48,500
Go home and get some rest

2495
01:56:48,500 --> 01:56:49,220
Rest

2496
01:56:49,740 --> 01:56:52,260
I want your report first thing tomorrow

2497
01:56:55,240 --> 01:56:56,440
Not coming to my place tonight?

2498
01:56:56,680 --> 01:56:57,280
No

2499
01:57:00,870 --> 01:57:02,070
I've sensed it too

2500
01:57:02,190 --> 01:57:03,510
Your recent tastes

2501
01:57:03,950 --> 01:57:04,870
Have changed a little

2502
01:57:06,460 --> 01:57:07,740
It's rather sad to say

2503
01:57:08,300 --> 01:57:09,780
He suffers from ED

2504
01:57:10,260 --> 01:57:11,300
He can't get it up

2505
01:57:12,170 --> 01:57:13,090
To protect himself

2506
01:57:13,090 --> 01:57:14,730
From being hurt by reality

2507
01:57:15,300 --> 01:57:18,340
His brain triggers a defense mechanism

2508
01:57:18,660 --> 01:57:20,420
To fill in his own night of passion

2509
01:57:20,420 --> 01:57:22,100
His brain auto-triggers that defense

2510
01:57:22,420 --> 01:57:24,300
To complete his night of passion

2511
01:57:24,300 --> 01:57:28,260
He's truly terrifying

2512
01:57:28,260 --> 01:57:29,260
No

2513
01:57:29,260 --> 01:57:32,640
He might be an anti-revisionist

2514
01:57:32,640 --> 01:57:34,640
A restless creed in his heart

2515
01:57:34,640 --> 01:57:36,640
But he has nothing

2516
01:57:36,640 --> 01:57:39,640
No gift, no talent

2517
01:57:39,640 --> 01:57:41,640
And only a scrap of courage

2518
01:57:41,640 --> 01:57:45,180
In this world full of injustice

2519
01:57:45,180 --> 01:59:55,020
What is he supposed to do?

2520
01:59:55,020 --> 01:59:57,120
Did you think the play was good?

2521
01:59:57,120 --> 01:59:58,120
It was awful

2522
01:59:58,120 --> 01:59:59,120
What a piece of junk

2523
01:59:59,120 --> 02:00:02,120
But I kind of loved it

2524
02:00:02,120 --> 02:00:05,300
I like bad plays

2525
02:00:05,300 --> 02:00:07,300
Because I'm a bad person

2526
02:00:07,300 --> 02:00:09,660
What's a good play anyway?

2527
02:00:09,660 --> 02:00:11,660
There are none. I've never seen one

2528
02:00:11,660 --> 02:00:15,190
Bad people watch bad plays

2529
02:00:15,190 --> 02:00:17,190
Good people watch good plays

2530
02:00:17,190 --> 02:00:19,190
It was wonderful. I loved it

2531
02:00:19,190 --> 02:00:21,190
My god, I saw a world of ice

2532
02:00:21,190 --> 02:00:23,190
It was like seeing my mother

2533
02:00:23,190 --> 02:00:26,020
So warm

2534
02:00:26,020 --> 02:00:28,020
My favorite play of my whole life

2535
02:00:30,020 --> 02:00:34,710
A few questions for you

2536
02:00:34,710 --> 02:00:38,120
Go ahead

2537
02:00:38,120 --> 02:00:40,120
Would you give everything for your ideals?

2538
02:00:40,120 --> 02:00:45,060
Yes

2539
02:00:45,060 --> 02:00:46,060
Talking money is vulgar

2540
02:00:46,060 --> 02:00:48,410
That's not something I can reveal

2541
02:00:48,410 --> 02:00:53,790
Been doing any of that lately?

2542
02:00:53,790 --> 02:00:54,790
It's alright

2543
02:00:54,790 --> 02:00:55,790
Alright, huh?

2544
02:00:55,790 --> 02:01:03,480
If you went to a hooker, what kind would you pick?

2545
02:01:03,480 --> 02:01:04,480
What kind?

2546
02:01:04,480 --> 02:01:07,300
A good figure

2547
02:01:07,300 --> 02:01:09,590
And what kind of service?

2548
02:01:09,590 --> 02:01:19,270
Are you an idealist?

2549
02:01:19,270 --> 02:01:21,490
I think I am

2550
02:01:21,490 --> 02:01:22,490
I absolutely am

2551
02:01:22,490 --> 02:01:30,080
I am

2552
02:01:30,080 --> 02:01:37,680
Which one do I face?

2553
02:01:37,680 --> 02:01:38,680
Film him, film him, film him

2554
02:01:38,680 --> 02:01:40,280
Watching Iceberg

2555
02:01:40,280 --> 02:01:41,280
Film him!

2556
02:01:41,280 --> 02:01:42,880
Say it to both cameras

2557
02:01:42,880 --> 02:01:45,280
I... I think I

2558
02:01:45,280 --> 02:01:46,280
Yu Haoran

2559
02:01:46,280 --> 02:01:47,280
You tell me

2560
02:01:47,280 --> 02:01:49,660
I... I think

2561
02:01:49,660 --> 02:01:50,660
Zhang Yuming

2562
02:01:50,660 --> 02:01:55,860
What... what do I even say?

2563
02:01:55,860 --> 02:01:57,260
Chu Yixu

2564
02:01:57,260 --> 02:01:58,260
I am

2565
02:01:58,260 --> 02:02:00,030
Li Junjiang

2566
02:02:00,030 --> 02:02:02,630
Zhang Naizhu

2567
02:02:02,630 --> 02:02:06,280
I think I am

2568
02:02:06,280 --> 02:02:07,730
Good

2569
02:02:07,730 --> 02:02:11,760
And our two behind-the-scenes creators

2570
02:02:11,760 --> 02:02:12,760
Li Zuchang

2571
02:02:12,760 --> 02:02:14,760
We're a short-film collective

2572
02:02:14,760 --> 02:02:17,020
Press it again

2573
02:02:17,020 --> 02:02:19,020
Yep, it didn't record

2574
02:02:19,020 --> 02:02:21,020
Oh, the west

2575
02:02:21,020 --> 02:02:23,020
Again, again, again

2576
02:02:23,020 --> 02:02:25,020
Exactly right — come on

2577
02:02:25,020 --> 02:02:27,020
I

2578
